From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: win32u: a maximized position is the primary monitor's, moved to the window's

David 2026-11-16: a Linux program maximized on the second screen ended up
on the first. Its frame (a program drawing its own title bar) answers
WM_GETMINMAXINFO as Windows programs do, with its maximized position
relative to the monitor: the top left of the work area, 0,0. win32u took
the position a window gave as a point on the screen, so on the second
monitor it was maximized at 0,0, on the first. On Windows ptMaxSize and
ptMaxPosition are the primary monitor's, and the window manager moves
them to the monitor the window is on (MINMAXINFO's documentation). A
position the window changed now moves by the offset of its monitor from
the primary one; one it left alone is adapted as before. Chromium, WPF
and other programs that handle WM_GETMINMAXINFO on a second monitor are
maximized there too.

Gate: test-maxmon (headless sg-compositor, two outputs: a framed Linux
window maximized on the second monitor fills it, restores where it was;
on the first fills the first). test-multimon passes. Mutant
SG_MUTANT_MAXPOS_ABSOLUTE.

--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -4661,6 +4661,7 @@
     RECT rc_work, rc_primary;
     LONG adjusted_style;
     MINMAXINFO minmax;
+    POINT max_pos_before;
     INT xinc, yinc;
     RECT rc;
     WND *win;
@@ -4706,9 +4707,27 @@
         if (!empty_point( win->max_pos )) minmax.ptMaxPosition = win->max_pos;
         release_win_ptr( win );
     }
+    max_pos_before = minmax.ptMaxPosition;
 
     send_message( hwnd, WM_GETMINMAXINFO, 0, (LPARAM)&minmax );
 
+    /* Stained Glass OS: a position the window gave is, as on Windows, where it
+     * would be maximized on the primary monitor, and the window manager moves
+     * it to the monitor the window is on. Taken as a point on the screen, a
+     * window on the second monitor that says where it maximizes (0,0, the top
+     * left of its work area: a Linux program's frame, Chromium, WPF) was
+     * maximized on the first one (David 2026-11-16). */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_MAXPOS_ABSOLUTE
+    if (!(style & WS_CHILD) &&
+        (minmax.ptMaxPosition.x != max_pos_before.x || minmax.ptMaxPosition.y != max_pos_before.y))
+    {
+        MONITORINFO mon_info = monitor_info_from_window( hwnd, MONITOR_DEFAULTTOPRIMARY );
+        rc_primary = get_primary_monitor_rect( get_thread_dpi() );
+        minmax.ptMaxPosition.x += mon_info.rcMonitor.left - rc_primary.left;
+        minmax.ptMaxPosition.y += mon_info.rcMonitor.top - rc_primary.top;
+    }
+#endif
+
     /* if the app didn't change the values, adapt them for the current monitor */
 
     if (get_work_rect( hwnd, &rc_work ))
